  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>  can't be constant throughout the domain. Hence we can find  <math><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>  such that  <math><mi>ƒ</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math>  is one-one option  <math><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo></math>  is true.<br > <math><mo>(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>)</mo></math>   <math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&prime;</mi></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn><mi> </mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> <br > <math><mo>(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>)</mo></math>   <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msqrt><mn>85</mn><mi>x</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow></math>  satisfies given condition<br >But  <math><mrow><mrow><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">lim</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>∞</mi></mrow></munder></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msqrt><mn>85</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi> </mi><mi>D</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>E</mi></math> <br > <math><mo>⇒</mo><mi> </mi><mi> </mi></math> Incorrect<br > <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>D</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>   <math><mi>g</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&prime;</mi></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> <br > <math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&prime;</mi></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></math>      (by LMVT)<br > <math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></math>      (given)<br > <math><mo>⇒</mo><mi> </mi><mi> </mi><mi>g</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>≤</mo><mn>5</mn><mi> </mi><mi> </mi><mo>∃</mo><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4,0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> <br >Similarly  <math><mi>g</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>≤</mo><mn>5</mn><mi> </mi><mi> </mi><mo>∃</mo><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0,4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> <br > <math><mi>g</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>85</mn><mi> </mi><mo>⇒</mo><mi>g</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>  has maxima in  <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi> </mi><mi>α</mi></math> <br > <math><msup><mrow><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&prime;</mi></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi> </mi><mi>g</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>≥</mo><mn>85</mn></math> <br > <math><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&prime;</mi></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&prime;</mi><mi>&prime;</mi></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> <br >If  <math><msup><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&prime;</mi></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mi>g</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>≥</mo><mn>85</mn></math>  not possible<br > <math><mo>⇒</mo><mi> </mi><mi> </mi><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&prime;</mi><mi>&prime;</mi></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mi> </mi><mo>∃</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>∈</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4,4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>  <br > <math><mo>(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>)</mo></math>  correct",
